      "Wet-look sealers make stamped and exposed-aggregate decks look spectacular, and around a pool they carry a real safety cost. A glossy acrylic film on a wet surface is slippery in a way that matters when people are running on it in bare feet. If the appearance is the priority, the non-negotiable condition is a slip-resistant additive mixed into the sealer before application. Beyond the traction question, film-forming sealers around pools are more prone to clouding than elsewhere, because water sitting on the surface finds any weakness in the film.",
